.TH IMPERIAL-MARCH-GPIO 1 "2026-08-10" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imperial-march-gpio \- play an Imperial March motif on the local GPIO buzzer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imperial-march-gpio
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imperial-march-gpio
plays a short one-shot Imperial March motif on the configured local GPIO sound
pin. It is intended for later RFID card binding and respects the shared GPIO
sound mute file used by the local event-sound helpers.
.PP
The command uses RPi.GPIO, serializes playback through the shared sound-hook
lock file, and cleans the GPIO pin before exiting. By default it uses BCM GPIO
18, a conservative buzzer volume, and a one-octave transpose so the piezo can
reproduce the motif clearly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --pin " PIN"
GPIO BCM pin to use. Defaults to the local sound pin environment or 18.
.TP
.BI --volume " N"
Volume from 0.0 to 1.0. Defaults to
.B IMPERIAL_MARCH_VOLUME
or a conservative local sound-hook value.
.TP
.BI --tempo " BPM"
Tempo in beats per minute. Values are clamped to 30 through 320.
.TP
.BI --transpose " SEMITONES"
Transpose the motif by this many semitones. Defaults to 12.
.TP
.BI --repeat " N"
Number of times to play the motif. Values are clamped to 1 through 8.
.TP
.BI --gap " SECONDS"
Pause between repeats.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the note plan and total duration without touching GPIO.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Play once using the local GPIO default:
.EX
imperial-march-gpio
.EE
.TP
Preview without playing:
.EX
imperial-march-gpio --dry-run
.EE
.TP
Later bind the next unmapped RFID card to the command:
.EX
rfid-arm-next-script --script /home/arthe/.local/bin/imperial-march-gpio --display-name "IMPERIAL" --label-line1 "IMPERIAL" --label-line2 "MARCH"
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NODE_SOUND_GPIO_PIN, GWAY_SOUND_GPIO_PIN
Default BCM GPIO sound pin.
.TP
.B NODE_SOUND_GPIO_MUTE_FILE, GWAY_SOUND_GPIO_MUTE_FILE
Runtime mute flag. If present, the command exits successfully without playback.
.TP
.B IMPERIAL_MARCH_VOLUME, IMPERIAL_MARCH_TEMPO, IMPERIAL_MARCH_TRANSPOSE
Command-specific playback defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rfid-arm-next-script (1),
.BR gway-toggle-gpio-sound-mute (1)
